# [[.Name]]

[[.Title]]: [[.Summary]]. Generated by kickhub from `[[.Template]]` v[[.Version]], target **[[.Target]]**.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `internal/job/job.go` | `Run(ctx)`: your work goes here |
| `cmd/job` | Runs the job once and exits non-zero on failure |
| `Dockerfile` | The image every target runs |
[[ if eq .Target "aws" -]]
| `infra/` | ECS cluster, Fargate task definition, ECR repository, roles and logs |
[[- else if eq .Target "gcp" -]]
| `infra/` | Cloud Run job, registry and service account |
[[- else -]]
| `docker-compose.yml` | The job as a container |
[[- end ]]
| `.kickhub.yaml` | Records the template, version and parameters used |

## Run it

```sh
make test
make run            # one execution, locally
```
[[ if eq .Target "aws" ]]
```sh
make infra-apply    # cluster, task definition, repository, roles
make image          # builds and pushes :latest
make execute SUBNETS="$(aws ec2 describe-subnets --region [[.P.aws_region]] --filters Name=default-for-az,Values=true --query 'Subnets[].SubnetId' --output text | tr '\t' ',')"
aws logs tail "/ecs/[[.Name]]" --region [[.P.aws_region]] --follow
```

`make execute` above uses the default VPC's subnets. Pass your own subnet ids for a real environment. Give the job AWS permissions by attaching policies to the `task_role_name` output.
[[ else if eq .Target "gcp" ]]
```sh
make infra-apply                      # registry and service account
gcloud auth configure-docker [[.P.gcp_region]]-docker.pkg.dev
make image REPO="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw image_repository)"
make infra-apply IMAGE_URI="$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw image_repository):$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)"
make execute
```

The first `infra-apply` runs without an image and skips the job; the second creates it. Give the job permissions by granting roles to the `job_service_account` output.
[[ end ]]
To run this on a schedule instead, see the `scheduled-job` template.
